 | Constant lane masks (`Gen.mask_src` immediates) | A constant read as a lane mask is one bit per lane: lane L takes bit L. The 64-bit forms (`s_and/or/andn2_saveexec_b64`, `s_andn2_wrexec_b64`, `s_mov_b64`/`s_not_b64` into EXEC or VCC, `s_and/or/xor/andn2/orn2_b64` and `s_cselect_b64` on the lane-mask path) read the 64-bit value, an inline constant sign-extended (`-16` = lanes 4-63) and a literal with a zero high word, as `src64_data` reads 64-bit constants; the b32 forms (`s_*_saveexec_b32`, `s_andn2_wrexec_b32`) read the 32-bit value at bit L mod 32. 0 and -1 still give no lane and every lane, with no per-lane code. `s_bcnt0/1_i32_b64` and `s_ff0/1_i32_b64` of a constant read the constant's 64 bits via `src64_data` (scalar data: inline negative constants sign-extend to 64 bits, so `s_ff0_i32_b64 s0, -1` gives −1 rather than 32, and 32-bit literals zero-extend; CPU-checked in `tests/semantic/test_scalar_bitcmp.py`, **not yet GPU-verified**). `s_bcnt0/1_i32_b64` of a constant counts the constant's 64 bits (scalar data, like `s_ff0/1_i32_b64`). **Before this fix every lane took bit 0 of the constant**: `s_and_saveexec_b32 s7, 0xff00` with all 32 lanes on left none on, `5` left all 32 on, and `s_bcnt1_i32_b64 s0, 0xff00ff` gave 32. llvm-mc rejects a constant as the mask operand of `v_cndmask_b32_e64` / `v_add_co_ci_u32_e64` and decodes one as "Invalid immediate", so those VALU callers never see a constant. **A constant held in an SGPR** (`s_mov_b32 s20, 0x3ffffc00`) is read the same way when it reaches a mask consumer: `mask_src` takes bit L of an SGPR that `holds_lane_mask` doesn't flag (a pair in a wave64 64-bit context: the high SGPR for lanes 32-63). In a wave32 or wave64 program a 32-bit bitwise SALU op (`s_not_b32`, `s_and/or/xor/andn2/orn2/nand/nor/xnor_b32`, `s_cselect_b32`) that writes EXEC/VCC (`exec_lo`/`vcc_lo` in wave32; `exec_lo`/`exec_hi` and mask-holding `vcc_lo`/`vcc_hi` in wave64, including after `s_mov_b64 vcc, 0/-1`) skips scalar constant folding, reads its operands through `Gen._mask_b32_src` / `mask_src` (collecting the opposite half through `wave_mask` if a wave64 op mixes `lo` and `hi` halves), preserves the untouched half of EXEC/VCC in wave64 (`exec_half_write` / `put_mask`), and votes SCC over the wave (wave32) or that 32-lane half (wave64, `scc_any_half`), matching `s_not_b32` and the binary ops on lane-mask SGPRs too; into a plain SGPR with a constant it stays a data read, because `lane_masks.py` classifies that SGPR as data when the other operand is a constant (`s_and_b32 s20, exec_lo, 1` then `s_bcnt1` must count the wave's bits: found by @Pierre-Kookis on #1792, GPU-reproduced), and `s_mov_b32 exec_lo/exec_hi, sN` takes each lane's bit. In a wave32 program a 32-bit bitwise SOP2 (`s_and/or/xor/andn2/orn2/nand/nor/xnor_b32`, `s_cselect_b32`) that writes EXEC/VCC reads both operands through `mask_src` (`Gen.sop2_b32_srcs`); into a plain SGPR it stays a data read, because `lane_masks.py` classifies that SGPR as data when the other operand is a constant (`s_and_b32 s20, exec_lo, 1` then `s_bcnt1` must count the wave's bits: found by @Pierre-Kookis on #1792, GPU-reproduced), and `s_mov_b32 exec_lo/exec_hi, sN` takes each lane's bit. A real mask is unchanged: it holds 0 or ~0 per lane, and bit L of that is the same 0 or 1. Until 2026-11-22 these took the value whole, so `s_and_saveexec_b32 s6, s20` with that constant, or `s_and_b32 exec_lo, exec_lo, 0xff00`, left every lane on (found writing `cs_w32_saveexec_ext`, #1771; CPU-checked by `tests/semantic/test_mask_src_sgpr_const.py`, and `tools/cf_diff.py` / `tools/salu_diff.py` still pass). `s_not_b32` on lane masks, `s_and/or/xor_b32` with two immediates into `vcc_lo`, and wave64 half-mask bitwise ops (destination half preservation, `exec_hi`, and `scc_any_half`) are CPU-checked in `tests/semantic/test_salu_b32_lane_masks.py` (wave32, wave64, and `--wave64-emulate`, validated with `spirv-val`) and GPU-checked on gfx1036, RTX 5080 (`--wave64-emulate`), and RX 9060 XT (RADV). Not covered here: a b32 op on one half of a wave64 mask, masks read as data (#293), and a literal with bit 31 set in a 64-bit position (zero- vs sign-extension not measured). GPU-checked with `runtime/test/shaders/cs_w32_mask_imm.asm` and `cs_w64_mask_imm.asm` on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 (driver 616.92; wave64 with `LEONIDA_W64_EMULATE=1`) and an AMD Radeon RDNA2 iGPU (driver 26.10.1, native 64-wide subgroup): both failed before on both GPUs. Run across every lane in `tests/semantic/test_value_semantics.py` (`LaneMaskConstants`). |
 | Scalar select and pack (`s_cmov_b32`, `s_cmovk_i32`, `s_pack_ll/lh/hh_b32_b16`) | `s_cmov_b32` / `s_cmovk_i32`: D = SCC ? S0 : D (`s_cmovk_i32`'s S0 is the 16-bit immediate, sign-extended); SCC is read, not written; the destination must be an SGPR (a lane-mask destination, and `s_cmov_b64`, stay `Unsupported`, #210). `s_pack_*`: the low half of D from S0, the high half from S1, the letters naming the half of each (l = 15:0, h = 31:16), S0 first; GFX10 has no `s_pack_hl`; SCC not written. Source: RDNA2 ISA SOP1/SOP2/SOPK. CPU-checked by `tests/semantic/test_salu_cmov.py` and `test_salu_pack.py`; the translated shaders were run on NVIDIA by reviewers (`s_cmov*`: RTX 5090, RTX 4050 and Radeon 740M in #613; `s_pack_*`: RTX 5090 in #449). **Hardware-verified on RDNA2** (`gfx1035`, wave32 and wave64 via `tools/int_hw_probe.py --oracle both`, SHADER-137, SCC kept). |
